# Lab 20: Companion registration delete experiment
#
# Question:
# After an approved disposable GCP source agent is deleted and Registry Sync
# confirms its absence, can the mapped companion Registration and its dedicated
# Agent Identity be retired safely and independently?
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Parts 1 and 2 are read-only. Parts 3 and 4 are optional, destructive, and
# require separate approval. Registration deletion is irreversible.
# Agent Identity deletion is soft deletion; it is not permanent purge.
#
# Put all real values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
# A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<registry-sync-package-id>
# A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID=<platform-blueprint-app-id>
# A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID=<dedicated-agent-identity-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID=<companion-registration-id>
#
# Save private responses only under:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/
#
# This file never deletes the platform Blueprint or Registry Sync connection.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@expectedSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@agentIdentityId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID}}
@companionRegistrationId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@readAccessToken = {{$aadV2Token scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/CopilotPackages.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.Read.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}
@dependencyReadToken = {{$aadV2Token new scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/Application.Read.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}
@registrationDeleteToken = {{$aadV2Token new scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/CopilotPackages.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}
@identityDeleteToken = {{$aadV2Token new scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.DeleteRestore.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1 - Confirm the signed-in operator
#
# Expected: 200. Sending this request triggers REST Client authentication.

# @name deleteCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Capture complete Package inventory before provider deletion
#
# Expected: 200. Read every returned page and locate the original Package using
# its exact scoped provider source key, not display name alone.

# @name deleteListPackagesBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.3 - Capture the original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm its nested provider sourceAgentId equals the exact
# value saved in A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID.

# @name deleteGetOriginalPackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.4 - Capture the mapped companion Registration
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - ID equals A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
# - sourceAgentId equals the legacy value created by the earlier experiment:
#   committed-fleet:companion:v1:gcp:<exact-provider-source-id>
# - do not delete solely to replace that legacy namespace
# - Blueprint and Agent Identity links match the durable mapping

# @name deleteGetRegistrationBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.5 - Capture the mapped Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm the ID and Blueprint appId match the mapping.

# @name deleteGetIdentityBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.6 - OPTIONAL inspect direct app-role assignments
#
# This documented service-principal relationship requires the separately
# consented Application.Read.All permission. Do not request broader permission
# solely to make this experiment pass. If this read is not already approved,
# classify dependency inspection as unavailable and stop before deletion.
#
# Expected when approved: 200. A non-empty response requires dependency
# review; it is not authorization to remove assignments or delete the identity.

# @name deleteGetIdentityAppRoleAssignments
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/appRoleAssignments
Authorization: Bearer {{dependencyReadToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.7 - Inspect direct directory memberships
#
# Expected: 200. Record only safe counts/classifications in tracked evidence.

# @name deleteGetIdentityMemberships
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity/memberOf?$select=id,displayName
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual provider checkpoint - no request
#
# Only with explicit approval, delete the existing disposable GCP source agent
# through its supported provider interface.
#
# Record private provider evidence, then wait for:
# - a successful Registry Sync cycle;
# - the agreed propagation/grace period; and
# - a healthy connection with no permission or connector errors.
#
# Provider deletion alone does not authorize companion cleanup. Continue with
# the read-only Registry Sync observations below.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.1 - Read complete Package inventory after provider deletion and sync
#
# Expected: 200. Read every page.
#
# Search by the exact scoped provider source key:
# - If the same key has a new Package ID, update the mapping and STOP.
# - If the original Package or another matching source remains, STOP.
# - If inventory is partial or the connector is unhealthy, STOP.

# @name deleteListPackagesAfterSourceDeletion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 2.2 - Probe the previous Package ID
#
# Expected only after confirmed source deletion: 404.
#
# A 200 means the Package still exists and cleanup must stop. A 404 by itself
# is not sufficient; Part 2.1, sync health, grace period, and provider evidence
# must also agree.

# @name deleteGetOriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop A - confirm source retirement before deleting companion objects
#
# Continue only when all conditions are true:
# - the provider confirms the exact disposable source agent was deleted;
# - successful Registry Sync plus the grace period confirms the scoped source
#   key is absent from every Package List page;
# - no replacement Package exists for the same source key;
# - the mapping still identifies exactly one companion Registration and Agent
#   Identity for that source;
# - no other active mapping references either object;
# - runtime use, grants, policies, memberships, owners, and other dependencies
#   have been reviewed; and
# - separate Registration retirement approval has been recorded.
#
# Otherwise mark reconciliation-required and stop.

###############################################################################
# Part 3.1 - OPTIONAL irreversible companion Registration deletion
#
# Do not send during evidence gathering.
# Expected: 204.

# @name deleteCompanionRegistration
DELETE {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{registrationDeleteToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.2 - Confirm the Registration is gone
#
# Run only after Part 3.1 returned 204.
# Expected: 404.

# @name deleteGetRegistrationAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.3 - Observe Package inventory after Registration deletion
#
# Expected: 200. Do not assume the companion Package disappears immediately
# or that its lifecycle matches the original Registry Sync Package.

# @name deleteListPackagesAfterRegistrationDeletion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.4 - Confirm the Agent Identity still exists independently
#
# Expected: 200. Registration deletion does not prove that Agent Identity
# deletion is safe or automatic.

# @name deleteGetIdentityAfterRegistrationDeletion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop B - separately approve Agent Identity retirement
#
# Continue only when:
# - Part 3.1 and Part 3.2 proved Registration deletion;
# - Package observations have been recorded;
# - the Agent Identity was created exclusively for this source;
# - no runtime binding, app-role assignment, membership, grant, policy, owner
#   workflow, or other consumer still requires it; and
# - Agent Identity retirement approval has been recorded.
#
# Keep the platform Blueprint. Do not delete it as per-agent cleanup.

###############################################################################
# Part 4.1 - OPTIONAL Agent Identity soft deletion
#
# Expected: 204. This does not permanently purge the directory object.

# @name deleteAgentIdentity
DELETE {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{identityDeleteToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 4.2 - Confirm the active Agent Identity is gone
#
# Run only after Part 4.1 returned 204.
# Expected: 404 from the active typed resource.
#
# Do not interpret this as permanent purge. Retain the ID and deletion
# timestamp in the tombstone for restore, retention, and audit decisions.

# @name deleteGetIdentityAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Final tombstone checkpoint - no request
#
# Preserve:
# - tenant, platform, provider scope, and exact provider sourceAgentId
# - former Package, companion Registration, Agent Identity, and Blueprint IDs
# - provider deletion and Registry Sync confirmation timestamps
# - Registration DELETE/GET outcomes
# - Agent Identity DELETE/GET outcomes
# - dependency-review and approval references
# - final status and any partial or inconclusive result
#
# Do not erase the mapping. It prevents stale inventory from silently creating
# a replacement companion. Do not delete the shared platform Blueprint,
# Registry Sync connection, provider credentials, or unrelated local evidence.
